# MarketAdvisor: its texts, in English. Godot shows English for any language without its own file (its fallback
# locale), so another language only needs a copy of this file with its Language and msgstr lines translated, loaded in
# ModMain.gd. Keep each %s, and each %% (a percent sign): the code fills them in.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: en\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"

# The station menu's Mineral Market entry with its alert mark, while a trade is due; %s is the entry's own text.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_ALERT"
msgstr "%s (*)"

# The tooltip of the Shift badge beside the Mineral Market's Trade button; the first %s is the key to hold while
# clicking the button, the second the mod's name.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SETTINGS_TOOLTIP"
msgstr "Click the button while pressing %s to open the %s settings."

# The same while the game is played with a gamepad; the first %s is the button to press on the highlighted Trade
# button, the second the one to hold, the third the mod's name.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SETTINGS_TOOLTIP_PAD"
msgstr "Highlight the button and press %s while holding %s to open the %s settings."

# The settings screen. Each setting has its name and, under the same key followed by SettingsUI.gd's
# DESCRIPTION_SUFFIX, the description the screen shows while it is selected, written as the game's Tuning descriptions
# are. A %s is the mineral the setting is about.

# The cash group: the notation switch, the two sliders that make the cash reserve, the slider of its tolerance, and the
# row under them.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_GROUP_CASH"
msgstr "Cash reserve"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SCIENTIFIC"
msgstr "Use scientific notation"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SCIENTIFIC_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Shows the cash reserve in scientific notation, such as 5e5, instead of thousands, millions and billions, such as "
"500K."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_AMOUNT"
msgstr "Amount"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_AMOUNT_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The cash reserve is this amount times the power of ten below.\n"
"\n"
"The Trade button at the bottom of the Mineral Market buys ore when your cash rises above the tolerance's range "
"around it, and sells that ore when your cash falls below that range. Either way, your cash ends up within one "
"tonne's price above it. At 0, all your cash goes into ore."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_POWER"
msgstr "Power of ten"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_POWER_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The power of ten the amount above is multiplied by.\n"
"\n"
"Together they make the cash reserve, shown under them with the tolerance's range."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_TOLERANCE"
msgstr "Tolerance"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_TOLERANCE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"How far your cash can drift above or below the cash reserve before the Trade button trades.\n"
"\n"
"While your cash stays in that range, a repair or a sale doesn't make it sell ore at a bad price, or buy ore at a "
"high one, just to match the cash reserve. Once your cash leaves the range, the trade brings it back to the cash "
"reserve. At 0, any difference of a tonne's price is traded."

# The name of the row under the sliders, whose value is the cash reserve, with the tolerance's range
# (MARKETADVISOR_RANGE) unless the tolerance is 0.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CASH_TOTAL"
msgstr "Cash reserve"

# The cash reserve's range, wherever the cash reserve is shown; the first %s is the bottom of the range, the second the
# top.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_RANGE"
msgstr "%s - %s"

# The trading group.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_GROUP_TRADE"
msgstr "Trading"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_TRADE_ALL"
msgstr "Trade all ores"

# %s: the mineral cash goes into while the switch is off.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_TRADE_ALL_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Lets the Trade button keep your cash in every ore, not only %s: it buys the ores furthest below their average on "
"the chart, and sells those furthest above.\n"
"\n"
"The cheapest ores' small tonnes bring your cash close to the cash reserve. Your trading also spreads over all ores: "
"the more of one ore you trade, the more its price swings in the months after."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SELL_ORE"
msgstr "Sell stored ore"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SELL_ORE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The Trade button also sells the ore you bring back from your dives, on the best day before your ship is ready, as "
"the price charts forecast it. The ore it bought to keep your cash in isn't sold this way.\n"
"\n"
"At the end of a dive, pick Store Minerals instead of Sell all, so the ore can wait for that day. Oddities are sold "
"either way. With Trade all ores, the cash goes back into ore."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_ALERT_ENTRY"
msgstr "Mark the Mineral Market entry"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_ALERT_ENTRY_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Puts (*) after the Mineral Market entry of the station menu while the Trade button has trades to make.\n"
"\n"
"Switch it off if you'd rather check the market yourself, or if another mod marks that entry too. The Trade button "
"works the same either way."

# The caption of the row in the Mineral Market's header, under your cash, with what the ore the Trade button bought to
# keep your cash in would sell for today. The value follows it in a label of its own, with a gap the mod adds.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_PARKED"
msgstr "Parked in ore:"

# The row at the bottom of the Mineral Market: the button, and the advice. A mineral is written as the market writes
# it (Be, W, Fe…).
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_TRADE"
msgstr "Trade"

# A mineral's tonnes; the first %s is the tonnes, the second the mineral.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_TONNES"
msgstr "%s t %s"

# The trades to make now; %s is their tonnes.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SELL"
msgstr "Sell %s."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_BUY"
msgstr "Buy %s."

# %s: the cash once the trades are made.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_LEAVES"
msgstr "Leaves %s E$."

# A trade worth waiting for, before your ship is ready; the first %s is the mineral, the second the date.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_WAIT_SELL"
msgstr "Sell %s on %s: the chart forecasts a higher price."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_WAIT_BUY"
msgstr "Buy %s on %s: the chart forecasts a lower price."

# %s: a mineral the advice sells well below its average price on the chart.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_WARN"
msgstr "%s sells well below its average on the chart."

# The minerals cash goes into are full; the first %s is them, the second the most the market lets you hold.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_CAPPED"
msgstr "No more room: %s at %s t."

# %s: the cash reserve.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SHORT"
msgstr "Not enough ore to sell for a cash reserve of %s E$."

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_AT_FLOOR"
msgstr "Nothing to trade. Cash reserve: %s E$."

# The line comparing today's prices with the average of each chart's history; %s is the minerals.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_VS_AVERAGE"
msgstr "Today against the chart's average: %s."

# A mineral in that line; the first %s is the mineral, the second the percentage.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_LOWER"
msgstr "%s %s %% lower"

msgid "MARKETADVISOR_HIGHER"
msgstr "%s %s %% higher"

# %s: the mineral.
msgid "MARKETADVISOR_SAME"
msgstr "%s the same"
